# TP Reviews Engine - code owners.
#
# TR-CI-005: review is required for src/core/, schemas/, selectors/, and
# compliance/. Those four are not a seniority signal; each is a place where a
# plausible-looking change does damage that is invisible at the diff.
#
# Last matching pattern wins.

* @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- The pure kernel ---
# Fifteen property laws depend on these modules being deterministic. A single
# Date.now() default parameter voids all fifteen without failing anything.
/src/core/ @Vanshmodi-dev

# The three D4/D5 modules inside it, called out separately so a reviewer knows
# which kind of change they are looking at before they open the diff:
#   reconcile/  absence is not deletion. The only defect that can silently
#               wipe a paying client's reviews.
#   normalize/  removes markup rather than escaping it. The security boundary
#               for every client website simultaneously.
#   gate/       decides whether anything reaches a visitor at all. 100%
#               coverage, no short-circuit evaluation.
/src/core/reconcile/ @Vanshmodi-dev
/src/core/normalize/ @Vanshmodi-dev
/src/core/gate/ @Vanshmodi-dev
/src/core/identity/ @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- The public contract ---
# A payload schema change is visible to every client website that reads it.
# Breaking it is not a deploy, it is a migration.
/schemas/ @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- Volatile knowledge ---
# A merged pack is never edited; a change creates v<n+1>.json. Editing one in
# place silently rewrites what every historical fixture is tested against.
/selectors/ @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- Authorisations and suppressions ---
# denylist.json carries erasure obligations, and an authorisation record is the
# evidence that a listing may be harvested at all.
/compliance/ @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- The single point of secret handling and log redaction ---
/src/infra/logger/redact.mjs @Vanshmodi-dev

# --- Automation that holds a write token ---
/.github/ @Vanshmodi-dev
